 "internal_silences": [],
 "text": "Everyone makes mistakes. What matters is what we do after we make them. When something goes wrong at work, I ask three questions. What happened? Why did it happen? What will I do differently next time? I write the answers down, because writing makes my thinking clear. I try to focus on the process, not on blame. Most mistakes come from unclear steps, not from careless people. When I share what I learned, others can avoid the same problem. Over time, a team that talks openly about mistakes makes far fewer of them. Mistakes are a normal part of any real work, and each one carries a lesson if we look for it."
